# Cloudflare Pages direct-upload only ever excludes node_modules, .DS_Store
# and .git on its own. Everything else here is public if it reaches the
# upload directory, so this file names everything besides what scripts/
# stage.js actually copies (index.html, app.css, 404.html, robots.txt, js/,
# and the generated type directories and sitemap.xml) that must never ship.
#
# CAVEAT, checked against the exact wrangler build this project's CI fetches
# (wrangler 4.129.0, via `npx -y wrangler@latest`): the classic
# `wrangler pages deploy` code path (src/pages/upload.ts's `validate`
# function) walks the deploy directory against a hardcoded IGNORE_LIST
# (_worker.js, _redirects, _headers, _routes.json, functions, .DS_Store,
# node_modules, .git, .wrangler) and does not read a `.pagesignore`,
# `.gitignore`, or `.assetsignore` file at all. This file therefore has no
# effect on that path today. (A separate, newer path that delegates new
# projects to Workers static assets does honor `.assetsignore`, but only
# when wrangler detects it is being driven by an AI coding agent, which a
# plain GitHub Actions runner is not.)
#
# The actual fix is in .github/workflows/deploy.yml: it stages only the
# allowlisted files and directories (see scripts/stage.js) into a public/
# directory and deploys that directory instead of the repo root, so nothing
# below can leak regardless of which upload path wrangler takes. This file is
# kept anyway, in case a future wrangler version reads it, and to document
# exactly what must never be public.
#
# scripts/stage.js is what actually enforces this allowlist now, and
# test/stage.test.js asserts it.
docs/
test/
scripts/
.github/
package.json
.gitignore
.superpowers/
.pagesignore
